  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 336 AM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nMoving into Thursday and Friday, the longwave trough \ndeamplifies and largely shears out as an approaching northern \nstream wave aids in pushing this system away from the area. For \nsensible weather, this will mean the rain ending from early \nThursday or perhaps as soon as Wednesday night over northwestern\nIowa and our northwest forecast area. This drying trend moves \nslowly southeastward ending the rain in our southeastern \nforecast area by Friday morning.The approaching northern stream \nwave will move through Saturday and will bring a return of some \nclouds and atmospheric moisture return, but showers seem more \nlimited and would certainly be progressive. Behind this system, \nnorthwesterly flow looks to take over and with a zone of high \npressure moving in, this may spell a change as we continue into \nOctober with some drier conditions.",
